From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: d012 setup <setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] worker_priority keeps windows.h's far and near macros out

windows.h defines near and far as empty macros; the header now reaches the renderer, whose frame interpolation check has a lambda named far, so the Windows build failed with C2513.
---

diff --git a/host/worker_priority.hpp b/host/worker_priority.hpp
index 081bd24..0f5aca5 100644
--- a/host/worker_priority.hpp
+++ b/host/worker_priority.hpp
@@ -12,6 +12,9 @@
 #define WIN32_LEAN_AND_MEAN
 #define NOMINMAX
 #include <windows.h>
+// windows.h defines near and far as empty macros, which break any later code that names a variable "far".
+#undef near
+#undef far
 #elif defined(__linux__) || defined(__ANDROID__)
 #include <sys/resource.h>
 #include <sys/syscall.h>
